  "description": "Zinc is the corrosion protection metal. Without galvanizing, steel structures rust and fail \u2014 a bare steel bridge in a marine atmosphere loses 50-100 \u03bcm/year of section thickness and becomes structurally unsafe within 10-20 years. Zinc sacrifices itself electrochemically to protect steel (electrode potential -0.76 V vs. SHE, compared to iron's -0.44 V). A galvanized coating of 85 \u03bcm provides 50-100+ years of service in rural atmospheres. No other common metal offers this combination of low co...",
